WEBVTT

00:07:28.011 --> 00:07:31.348
So even if we were able to,
say, implement a tool

00:07:31.381 --> 00:07:34.217
that would bring more women
into upper management,

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:39.022
it's highly likely that we would still
evaluate the performance of those women

00:07:39.055 --> 00:07:41.124
with biased perceptions.

00:07:41.157 --> 00:07:44.594
Clearly, leadership and likability
should not be mutually exclusive

00:07:44.627 --> 00:07:46.429
for women or for men.

00:07:46.463 --> 00:07:48.465
So how do we solve for this dilemma?

00:07:49.232 --> 00:07:52.902
I wish I could offer you
a cure to unconscious bias.

00:07:52.902 --> 00:07:54.337
I don't believe there is one.

00:07:55.338 --> 00:07:57.874
But we need to disrupt stereotypes

00:07:57.907 --> 00:08:01.678
and redefine what it is
to be a leader and a woman.